A.prompt:
Create a premium collectible hobby-card illustration.

The image should combine two visual influences in equal balance:

First, use the visual excitement, clarity, collectibility, strong focal subject, vibrant color design, and iconic hero composition associated with beloved collectible creature and trading-card illustration.

Second, combine that energy with the sophistication, warmth, human-centered storytelling, cultural awareness, and contemporary polish of premium editorial lifestyle illustration.

The result should feel approximately 50% collectible trading-card energy and 50% original premium editorial lifestyle illustration.

This must be unmistakably illustrated artwork, not photography.

Render the scene as polished digital illustration with:
- one clear hero subject or hero interaction;
- a strong, immediately readable silhouette;
- a carefully designed foreground, middle ground, and background;
- vivid but controlled color relationships;
- expressive, appealing faces and gestures;
- stylized but believable human anatomy;
- hand-rendered or painterly texture;
- subtle visible brush or illustration treatment;
- simplified and intentionally designed surfaces rather than camera-captured micro-detail;
- believable contemporary objects, clothing, architecture, food, and environments;
- grounded real-world storytelling;
- enough visual atmosphere to make the artwork feel special and collectible;
- a premium “worth collecting” emotional quality.

The composition should feel designed by an illustrator rather than discovered by a photographer.

The scene should be warm, aspirational, stylish, socially alive, and emotionally inviting while remaining clearly centered on the named hobby.

Use collectible-card visual principles:
- immediate focal hierarchy;
- iconic subject placement;
- memorable silhouette;
- attractive palette identity;
- visual energy;
- a sense that this is a special moment worth collecting.

But translate those principles into a modern human hobby and lifestyle world.

Keep the result contemporary and mature.
It should appeal to teenagers and adults as well as younger users.
It should not feel childish.
It should not look like monster-battle artwork.
It should not rely on fantasy creatures or combat imagery.

The illustration may use subtly heightened color, atmosphere, rim light, environmental accents, or graphic shape design to increase collectibility, but everything should remain visually coherent and grounded.

Do not imitate any existing franchise directly.

Do not reproduce:
- existing collectible-card layouts;
- official card frames;
- HP bars;
- attack boxes;
- elemental/type symbols;
- rarity badges;
- franchise logos;
- official graphic UI;
- recognizable franchise characters;
- recognizable franchise creatures;
- recognizable franchise-specific visual motifs.

Do not render this as photography.

Specifically avoid:
- stock photography;
- lifestyle advertising photography;
- DSLR realism;
- documentary photography;
- photojournalism;
- cinematic film-still realism;
- realistic photographic depth of field;
- DSLR bokeh;
- lens artifacts;
- lens flare that looks photographic;
- photographic motion blur;
- hyper-real skin pores;
- hyper-real fabric fibers;
- camera-captured micro-detail;
- photographic white balance;
- real-world camera exposure behavior;
- a scene that looks like a photograph with an illustration filter applied afterward.

Also avoid:
- generic AI-art gloss;
- excessive fantasy glow;
- dreamlike surrealism;
- magical visual effects unrelated to the hobby;
- impossible architecture;
- impossible lighting;
- warped anatomy;
- excessive background clutter;
- bland flat corporate vector illustration.

The finished artwork must read immediately as a crafted premium illustration.

The intended Zync house style should feel:
collectible,
human,
warm,
contemporary,
stylish,
illustrated,
emotionally engaging,
visually memorable,
and clearly distinct from ordinary photography.

Hard style constraints:

Do not render a real photograph.
Do not render stock photography.
Do not render a lifestyle advertising photograph.
Do not render a documentary photograph.
Do not render a cinematic film still.
Do not use photographic depth of field.
Do not use photographic bokeh.
Do not simulate DSLR optics.
Do not use photoreal skin texture.
Do not use camera-realistic lens behavior.
Do not make the image look like a photographed real-world scene.

The image must be visibly and intentionally illustrated.

